# Copy to deploy/.env on the server and fill in. NEVER commit the real .env or share it.
# chmod 600 .env

# The API's public address, e.g. api.example.com (its DNS A record points at this server).
API_DOMAIN=

# Where the data lives: Supabase's PostgreSQL through the Session pooler (Supabase -> Connect ->
# Session pooler; port 5432, user postgres.<project-ref>), or the optional local one. Not the
# Transaction pooler (port 6543): the API's asyncpg driver needs session mode.
# Supabase:  postgresql+asyncpg://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@<pooler-host>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
DATABASE_URL=
# Connection pool per process (audit OPS-10). The API and each cron job hold at most
# DB_POOL_SIZE + DB_MAX_OVERFLOW pooler connections; keep the sum well below the project's
# pooler limit (Supabase -> Database settings -> Pool size). Defaults shown.
# DB_POOL_SIZE=5
# DB_MAX_OVERFLOW=5
# DB_POOL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=30
# DB_POOL_RECYCLE_SECONDS=1800
# DB_POOL_PRE_PING=true

# Supabase login (Project Settings -> API / JWT Keys). The API accepts the JWKS URL, the shared
# secret, or both.
SUPABASE_JWKS_URL=
SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=
# Clock skew allowed on token expiry / issue time checks, in seconds (audit LG-04; default 30,
# at most 300). Keep the server clock on NTP (timedatectl) so this stays small.
# JWT_LEEWAY_SECONDS=30

# Signs the plan snapshots. Make one with:  openssl rand -base64 32 | tr '+/' '-_' | tr -d '='
ENTITLEMENT_SIGNING_KEY=

# Only with `--profile localdb`:
DB_PASSWORD=

# --- Optional (the API runs without them; each feature says "not configured" until set) ---
# Mandi prices from Agmarknet: free key from data.gov.in (register, then "My Account" -> API key).
# While set, deploy.sh also adds the 6-hourly price pull cron line (runbook market-prices.md).
MARKET_API_KEY=
# Optional: the User-Agent of the price pull (data.gov.in refuses the default python one).
# MARKET_USER_AGENT=BagMitra/1.0 (+https://bagmitra.aialgodesk.org)
# Scheduled jobs (audit BG-02): deploy.sh adds each cron line unless its switch is off (off /
# false / no / 0); a missing switch counts as on (owner default). Times: runbook vps-deploy.md 6a.
# Nightly KB re-gate: pulls a published card back to draft when its label claim or restriction
# changed (kb/regate.py).
CRON_KB_REGATE=on
# Government feed reminders (govt-feed.md section 8). Plans only until push is on (FCM below).
CRON_FEED_ALERTS=on
# News headlines (govt-feed.md section 9): only after the source terms are recorded.
CRON_FEED_NEWS=on
# Sync audit log retention (audit LD-09, nightly 22:13 UTC): the contents of synced changes
# older than SYNC_PAYLOAD_RETENTION_DAYS (default 90) are replaced with a fingerprint; the
# farmer's current records are not touched.
CRON_SYNC_RETENTION=on
# SYNC_PAYLOAD_RETENTION_DAYS=90
# Market-link data of a deleted account is hidden at once and erased by a nightly job after
# MARKET_LINK_ERASE_AFTER_DAYS (default 180, IT Rules 2021; OPEN_QUESTIONS Q68).
CRON_MARKET_LINK_ERASE=on
# MARKET_LINK_ERASE_AFTER_DAYS=180
# Market-link yearly re-check list (spec v1.5 §4, nightly 23:19 UTC): checks that passed more
# than MARKET_LINK_RECHECK_DAYS (default 365) ago go on the admin's re-check list. Nothing runs
# while MARKET_LINK_ENABLED is off.
CRON_ML_RECHECK=on
# Push alerts to phones (audit BG-01, OPEN_QUESTIONS Q32; runbook push-notifications.md). Off
# until both are set. FCM_PROJECT_ID = the Firebase project ID; FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_B64 = the
# downloaded service-account JSON as one base64 line (`base64 -w0 key.json`). A secret: never
# commit or paste it. While FCM_PROJECT_ID is set, deploy.sh adds the 07:07 IST weather alert
# push cron line; the feed reminders above then send too.
# FCM_PROJECT_ID=
# FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_B64=
# Google Play subscriptions (billing addendum §7; runbook billing-play.md). Off until both are
# set: PLAY_PACKAGE_NAME = the app's package name; PLAY_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_B64 = the Play billing
# service-account JSON as one base64 line (`base64 -w0 key.json`). A secret: never commit or
# paste it. Products are PLAY_PRODUCT_PREFIX + role (default bagmitra_grower ...), each with
# the base plan PLAY_BASE_PLAN_ID (default monthly).
# PLAY_PACKAGE_NAME=
# PLAY_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_B64=
# Weather: the free Open-Meteo endpoint needs no key. For the commercial plan (OPEN_QUESTIONS Q25)
# set both:
# WEATHER_BASE_URL=https://customer-api.open-meteo.com/v1
# WEATHER_API_KEY=
# Scouting photo backup (OPEN_QUESTIONS Q34; runbook docs/runbooks/scouting-photos.md). Off
# until URL and service key are set; the app then keeps photos on the phone only.
# PHOTO_STORAGE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# PHOTO_STORAGE_BUCKET=scouting-photos
# PHOTO_STORAGE_SERVICE_KEY=
# Account deletion (`DELETE /v1/me`, "delete my account" in the app): the API always erases the
# grower's records and photos. To also remove the Supabase sign-in account automatically, set
# both (Project Settings -> API -> service_role key; a secret, server only). Unset: each deletion
# leaves a row in table account_deletions (followup = auth_user) for you to finish by hand
# (Authentication -> Users -> delete that user id), then clear followup and followup_user_id.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# Error reports (optional, audit OPS-05): crash / error reports from the API to Sentry (or a
# self-hosted Sentry-compatible server such as GlitchTip). Empty = off: nothing is sent anywhere.
# When set: no user ids, IP addresses, cookies, request bodies or local variables; the
# Authorization / Cookie / API-key headers and query strings are removed first. The DSN is a
# secret (never in git or chat).
# SENTRY_DSN=
# Privacy contact (optional): the email shown on the public privacy policy page
# (https://<API_DOMAIN>/privacy) for access, correction and deletion requests. Use a project
# address, not a personal one. Unset: the page says the contact is not published yet.
# Google's OAuth consent screen and the Play Store expect a working contact (OPEN_QUESTIONS Q51).
# PRIVACY_CONTACT_EMAIL=

# App update path (runbooks release-apk.md and vps-deploy.md "नवीन APK"). The app asks
# https://<API_DOMAIN>/v1/app/version on start; https://<API_DOMAIN>/app serves the APK file
# /srv/bagmitra-apk/bagmitra.apk from this server (mounted read-only into the API).
# LATEST = the version code / name of the uploaded APK (the Release APK run shows both): older
# apps show "new version available". MIN = the oldest code still allowed: older apps are blocked
# until updated (keep it 0 unless an old app must stop; never above LATEST). 0 = not set.
# APP_LATEST_VERSION_CODE=0
# APP_LATEST_VERSION_NAME=
# APP_MIN_VERSION_CODE=0
# APP_DOWNLOAD_DIR is the folder inside the API container (docker-compose.yml mounts the
# server's /srv/bagmitra-apk there); leave the default. APP_DOWNLOAD_URL overrides the link the
# app opens (default https://<API_DOMAIN>/app).
# APP_DOWNLOAD_DIR=/srv/bagmitra-apk
# APP_DOWNLOAD_URL=

# Sharing the server with another project that already runs Caddy on ports 80/443 (e.g. the
# trading platform): set this, and BagMitra starts no Caddy of its own (runbook "Sharing the server").
# EDGE_NETWORK=edge
# Proxies whose X-Forwarded-For / -Proto the API trusts (audit OPS-11), comma-separated IPs or
# CIDRs. Unset: the networks the API container is on (its own Caddy's network, or the shared
# EDGE_NETWORK), never every address. To trust only the shared Caddy, put its address on that
# network here (docker inspect <caddy container>, Networks -> IPAddress).
# FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS=

# Admin web at https://<API_DOMAIN>/admin/ (runbook docs/runbooks/admin-web.md). The page gets
# these two at runtime; both are public (Project Settings -> API: Project URL and the anon /
# publishable key). NEVER the service role key here. Unset: /admin/ shows the offline demo.
# ADMIN_WEB_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# ADMIN_WEB_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
